      "title": "Messages not syncing in Twake Chat after server restart",
      "issueSummary": "Messages appear to be missing or not syncing properly in Twake Chat after the server undergoes a restart.",
      "rawKnowledge": "Investigation revealed that in some cases, messages may appear to be missing in Twake Chat after a server restart due to a temporary sync delay or caching issue. The messages are not actually deleted but may not be visible until the next sync cycle. Users should refresh the chat or wait a few minutes for the sync to complete.",
      "whyPotentiallyRelevant": "The issue involves messages appearing to disappear in Twake Chat, which aligns with the user's experience of messages sometimes vanishing. The cause is not permanent and may be related to sync delays, similar to the user's observation of intermittent issues.",
      "sourceHint": "internal-knowledge-base/chat-sync-issues-post-restart"
    },
    {
      "title": "Chat messages not loading in Twake web app",
      "issueSummary": "Users report that chat messages do not load in the Twake web application, resulting in an empty chat interface.",
      "issueSummary": "Users report that chat messages do not load in the Twake web application, resulting in an empty chat interface.",
      "rawKnowledge": "This issue was observed in version 2.4.1 of the Twake web app. The problem was traced to a caching issue where the browser did not refresh the chat state after a message update. A fix was deployed that forced a cache clear on message updates. Users should ensure they are using the latest version of the app.",
      "whyPotentiallyRelevant": "The issue involves chat messages not being visible, which is similar to the user's report of messages sometimes disappearing. The root cause may be related to caching or sync delays, which could explain the intermittent nature of the problem.",
      "sourceHint": "internal-knowledge-base/chat-loading-issue-v2.4.1"
    }
  ]
}
